[cot:thought] Italy 2018 sold 3.6 GHz mid-band spectrum at about $0.40 per MHz-population. Germany 2019 raised ???6.55 billion.
[cot:thought] South Korea 2018 achieved rapid coverage growth despite lower per-unit pricing.
[cot:thought] Japan and China are
[cot:thought] included for coverage patterns. India 2022 raised roughly $19 billion in absolute proceeds. Brazil 2021 used lower prices with coverage obligations and reached about 95 percent coverage by 2024. France 2020 sold ???2.8 billion. Canada C-band reached approximately $1.6 billion. Saudi Arabia and the UAE show high coverage.
[cot:thought] Finland and Sweden had lower prices. The data structure is being organized. The data schema now
[cot:thought] includes country rows with auction type, regional grouping, and obligation intensity.
[cot:thought] Global proceeds by year, band averages, quadrant classification, and correlation statistics are also planned. Italy and Germany showed high per-MHz-population prices without guaranteed coverage leadership.
[cot:thought] Brazil combined low prices with coverage obligations to achieve strong coverage. The United States stands out as an outlier with both high prices and high coverage. India paid high absolute costs but built coverage more slowly. Ready to write the data file and commit phase one.
